=========================================================================
 META APP BACKGROUND BAN  -  Instagram + Threads
 packages : com.instagram.android
            com.instagram.barcelona   (Threads)
 date     : 2026-10-04
 policy   : keep user-launchable, but NO background activity ever
=========================================================================
WHAT THEY WERE DOING (why they messed with your background):
 - HeroKeepAliveService .................. kept the media/video process alive
                                           (a "keep-alive" that resists death)
 - IgBgFetchTaskLifeService + WorkManager  repeated background fetch jobs
                                           (SystemJobService fired every ~7-15s)
 - IgPushRegistrationService ............. re-registered push constantly
 - Broadcast receivers ................... reagistered to events to wake itself
 - Net effect: process stayed resident, thrashed swap (35k+ major page faults),
   pinned ~1-2 CPU cores OFF-SCREEN, held wake locks and burned heat.
=========================================================================
WHAT WE DID (verified on device)
=========================================================================
 [pm]     force-stop com.instagram.android   -> STOPPED
 [pm]     force-stop com.instagram.barcelona -> STOPPED
 [appops] RUN_IN_BACKGROUND      deny  (both)
 [appops] RUN_ANY_IN_BACKGROUND  deny  (both)
 [appops] WAKE_LOCK              deny  (both)
 [appops] START_FOREGROUND       deny  (both)
 [standby] bucket -> restricted = 45 (both)
 [doze]   deviceidle whitelist removed / absent (both)
 [log]    cpuinfo/top confirms processes no longer present
=========================================================================
WHAT THEY WON'T DO AGAIN
=========================================================================
 * No spawning background jobs / push re-registration / bg fetch.
 * No holding wake locks -> no keeping CPU/storage awake.
 * No starting foreground services on their own.
 * No surviving as a resident cached process to thrash swap.
 * -> less IO, less load, less HEAT, slower battery drain.
 STILL POSSIBLE (by design):
 * You CAN still launch them manually -> they run while on screen.
 * They die / stay frozen when you leave them (restricted bucket).
=========================================================================
TO RE-ENABLE BACKGROUND LATER (if ever wanted):
   cmd appops set com.instagram.android RUN_IN_BACKGROUND allow
   cmd appops set com.instagram.android RUN_ANY_IN_BACKGROUND allow
   cmd appops set com.instagram.android WAKE_LOCK allow
   cmd appops set com.instagram.android START_FOREGROUND allow
   cmd appops set com.instagram.barcelona RUN_IN_BACKGROUND allow
   cmd appops set com.instagram.barcelona RUN_ANY_IN_BACKGROUND allow
   cmd appops set com.instagram.barcelona WAKE_LOCK allow
   cmd appops set com.instagram.barcelona START_FOREGROUND allow
   am set-standby-bucket com.instagram.android active
   am set-standby-bucket com.instagram.barcelona active
=========================================================================
